  "question": {
    "text": "A body cools&nbsp;in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>minutes</mi></math> from<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. What will be its temperature after the next <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>minutes</mi></math>? The temperature of the surrounding is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>."
  },
